    "field_name": "Raw Output Example",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "sample_index,status,dmesg_nvidia_gpu_fault_xid_count,gpu_temperature_c,cuda_devices_visible,pcie_link_width_lanes,pcie_link_speed_gt_s,window_new_xid_count,sample_elapsed_s,sample_gpu_temperature_c,sample_cuda_devices_visible,sample_pcie_link_width_lanes,sample_pcie_link_speed_gt_s,error_message\n0,ok,0,42,1,16,32,0,0.0,41,1,16,32,"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Output Fields / Metrics to Parse",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "dmesg_nvidia_gpu_fault_xid_count, gpu_temperature_c, pcie_link_width_lanes, pcie_link_speed_gt_s, cuda_devices_visible, window_new_xid_count, sample_elapsed_s, sample_gpu_temperature_c, sample_cuda_devices_visible, sample_pcie_link_width_lanes, sample_pcie_link_speed_gt_s"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Parser and Normalization Notes",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "gpu_temperature_c is the peak, pcie_link_width_lanes and pcie_link_speed_gt_s the narrowest and slowest link, and cuda_devices_visible the fewest devices seen over the window, repeated on every row. sample_* columns hold each reading. dmesg_nvidia_gpu_fault_xid_count counts NVRM Xid lines since boot; na when dmesg is not readable"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Success Criteria",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "status=ok on every row: at least expected_gpu_count CUDA devices stayed visible, every GPU link stayed at least min_pcie_link_width lanes, and the threshold gates pass"
  },
